# PDF Generation Rules

## Architecture

All PDF generators must live under `lib/pdf/` and use the shared abstractions in `lib/pdf/core/`.

- Use `PdfDocumentBuilder` as the only entry point for creating a PDF document.
- Never instantiate `new jsPDF()` directly inside a feature-specific generator.
- Never draw headers, footers, logos, or page numbers manually – these are handled by the builder/template.

## Abstractions

| File | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| `core/pdfDocumentBuilder.ts` | jsPDF wrapper, page breaks, header/footer, fields, tables |
| `core/pdfSection.ts` | `PdfSection` interface and helper factory |
| `core/pdfLayout.ts` | Shared margins, fonts, colors, spacing |
| `core/pdfFormatters.ts` | Date, currency, percentage, enum, boolean formatters |

## Creating a new generator

1. Define the input type (model) in the relevant feature slice (`features/<slice>/<model>.model.ts`).
2. Create a dedicated generator file under `lib/pdf/<name>PdfGenerator.ts`.
3. Build the document with `const builder = await PdfDocumentBuilder.create({ title: '...', subtitle: '...' })`.
4. Add content using builder helpers: `sectionTitle`, `field`, `multiLineField`, `paragraph`, `table`, `renderSection`.
5. Call `builder.save(filename)` or return `builder.toBlob()` for preview.

## Sections

- Extract repeatable blocks (e.g. cargo info, address info) into `PdfSection` implementations under `lib/pdf/sections/`.
- A section must only depend on its own data and the builder; no direct jsPDF access.

## Formatting

- Dates: `formatDate` / `formatDateShort` / `formatDateTime`
- Currency: `formatCurrency(amount, currency)`
- Enums/labels: `formatEnum(value)`
- Booleans: `formatBoolean(value)`
- Quantities/dimensions: `formatQuantity`, `formatDimensions`

## Output

- Use `.save()` for user downloads.
- Use `.toBlob()` when the PDF needs to be previewed or uploaded.

## What to avoid

- Hardcoded magic numbers for margins, colors, or font sizes.
- Duplicated logo-loading or footer-drawing code.
- Mixing data transformation with rendering logic.
